## Docs

This project keeps three different kinds of documentation, each with its own purpose, scope, and lifecycle -- don't mix them up.

| Location | What it holds | Scope | Written by |
|---|---|---|---|
| `CONTEXT.md` | Project glossary -- resolved terminology only, no implementation details. | Project-wide (or one per bounded context, via `CONTEXT-MAP.md`); reused across every spec. | `domain-modeling` / `grill-with-docs` |
| `docs/adr/` | Architecture decision records -- hard-to-reverse, non-obvious decisions with a real trade-off behind them. | Project-wide, same lifecycle as `CONTEXT.md`. | `domain-modeling` |
| `docs/specs/<type>-<yyyy_mm>-<name>/` | One folder per spec (`<type>` is `feat`, `fix`, or `refactor`): `SPEC.md` (problem, solution, decisions), `plan/PLAN.md` (a seam-organized task breakdown), and `reports/` (one numbered file per `implement`/`debugger` run against it, e.g. `0001-implement.md`). | Per spec -- that piece of work's own task list and execution history, not shared with any other spec. | `/spec`, `implement`, `debugger` |
| `docs/build/` | Generated API docs (gitignored). | Rebuilt on demand. | `pdoc`, via `make docs` |

See [.claude/skills/spec/SKILL.md](.claude/skills/spec/SKILL.md) for the full spec-to-implementation workflow, and [.claude/skills/domain-modeling/SKILL.md](.claude/skills/domain-modeling/SKILL.md) for how `CONTEXT.md` and ADRs get built and maintained.

